+## Proposed actor/workflow backend increment (draft, 2026-10-04)
+
+### Architecture
+
+The optional operator-owned `actor-workflows.json` catalog adds versioned role
+behavior, stable Quant identity and finite workflow steps to the existing request
+path. RequestRuntime/AgentRequestBridge owns admission and queued work; released
+LangGraph StateGraph owns step ordering; the SDK agent graph owns bounded model
+steps. A Quant is distinct from job/child execution Agents and threads. The catalog
+does not mint Task/Agent/grant/CT47 authority. Native adapters retain their harness.
+Current tools remain existing granted reads; role and route ceilings cannot widen
+the host profile. New child effect namespaces preserve legacy default identities.
+
+### API
+
+Existing paired CT40 submit/get/cancel/resume capabilities remain. Authorized
+`get_agent_request` adds child `activities` with stable IDs/statuses/results.
+`cancel_agent_request` optionally accepts `activity_id`; cancelling a live/queued
+child cancels the dependent workflow through its existing cancellation owner.
+Revoked/stale disclosure authority withholds child content as well as job results.
+Cancellation is cooperative; uncertain shutdown owners report interruption.
+
+### Runbook and acceptance limits
+
+Configure existing `agent_sdk`, install the host catalog beside operator-config,
+start `python -m qma.daemon`, and use a matching ProductSession/current grants.
+Queued work survives unchanged restart. Interrupted work requires explicit resume;
+observed effects are reconciled rather than replayed. Same-version content mutation
+refuses; catalog replacement cannot retarget accepted jobs. Drain/recover under the
+old catalog before an upgrade. Leaf delegation and explicit child/model/node/time
+budgets apply. Actor memory shares only within exact principal/Quant/role/workflow/
+authority scope; no automatic global/app/session memory pool is implied.
+
+Full DeepAgents node harness adoption is the next recommended factory increment,
+not implemented by this draft. Current integration uses SDK skills middleware.
+LangMem extraction remains explicit and optional; generic graph tracing is disabled.
+See `_docwork/actor-workflow-architecture-api-runbook-draft.md` and the current
+requirements/evidence map for tested scope and remaining work. Local fixture tests
+do not establish whole-platform acceptance, live auth or remote endurance.
